  "term": "regional cerebral blood flow",
  "definition": "Regional cerebral blood flow is the amount or pattern of blood flow in specific areas of the brain. It is used to assess brain circulation, especially in ischemic cerebrovascular disease, and can help clarify the type of dementia.",
